<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff><font face="Tahoma" size="2">
I guess it's time I told you some of my background .. <p>
As you all know I am a wood elf.  We are a simple but proud and wise race, our lineage going back to the dawn of time.  We are the protectors of nature, the Great Mother Tunare.  
<p>
In the ancient times our forests spanned the world each holding a beauty that no words in any language can describe.  In those times there was a king, the most noble of all kings who's wisdom surpassed all save Tunare herself and who's teaching are still used to this day. Much was lost though in the days when Veeshan tore this world apart.  All we have is what is passed down from the elders to the young ones through fairy tales.  The king I spoke of is known to us in our native tongue as Eldaron which translates to the common tongue as "Elder King" his true name forever lost.  I took my name to honor his legend and the myth's that make us woodelves so proud.  Now that you know my name I can begin my story. 
<P>
I was born on a night when the moon was new. The great wolf spirit went to the druid council in their dreams and whispered to them of my birth .. a new brother; as it does when all druids are born.  It is custom that druids are raised by the druid council and so I was.  My youth was spent learning all of the secrets of nature.  Learning the languages of the different animals, trees and earth.  Learning what it is to be a druid.  My true mother and father I do not know all that well because shortly after I was taken away by my druid brothers, their village was attacked and everyone there either killed or enslaved by the clan Crushbone.  <br>
*grins evil transfixed on something that’s not here *<Br>
<br>I slay those simple minded orcs now when ever I can and let them know before their eyes close forever that I will not rest until their race is wiped clean from this world.  
<br>*sighs deeply* 
<br>I'm sorry, let me get back to my story. 
<br>
<br>
The day came when I needed to set out on my own.  Adventure was in my legs and I had to leave.  So here I was ready to go, I walk down from my guild hall to the lift.  I call the lift up and when it got to the top a half elf runs towards me his clothes torn,  by the looks of him he'd just been in a battle.  All he said was "those damn skellies broke my lute" then he passed out.  I used my art to healed him the best I could and he lived.  His name was and is Kalxen my best friend from that point on. We had many adventure together around Faydark and made many more friends.  Davar, Graynar, and Fanton were three guys that Kalxen and I traveled with often in those days.  <br>*stares off into the distance * <br> Those were good times.  <p>
The rest Norrath Militia knows.  <br><Br>
Thank you for taking the time to hear my story out.. good journeys to you and may Tunare bless you.<br><br>
~ El ~  



